WEBVTT

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.950
The Amatsumara isn't the only thing 
that makes your thoughts materialize!

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.100
That parfait that absorbed 
the power of the Amatsumara

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.410
also has the power to create, indeed.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.400
W-Wait a minute.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.170
We made all the people, too?

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.460
That's right. It's amazing, indeed.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.920
You can create people just by imagining them.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.140
Then the people who praised my drawings...

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.980
Yes, indeed.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:45.020
Your imagination created them, indeed.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.310
And our customers at Park...

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.150
Of course, indeed.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.200
Huh? What?

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.580
Wait a minute.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.820
You can't mean...

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.820
And Sayumin?

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.450
Yes, indeed.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:04.660
Your imaginations are 
truly powerful, indeed.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.460
You made Sayumin-san out of nothing...

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.920
and killed her yourselves.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:15.460
Sayumin never existed at all?

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:23.120
In other words, we've been inside 
a fantasy this whole time?

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.890
That's what you're saying, 
right, Misa-chan?

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:28.880
Fantasy?

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.620
It's all a fantasy, indeed!

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.760
Fantasy...

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:24.530
In other words, this isn't real?

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:25.640
That can't be.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.970
What's wrong, everyone?

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:32.940
This may seem amazing to you, but...

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.140
I can't believe we just imagined 
everything that happened.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.800
Well, uh...

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.250
It's not all fantasy.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:50.450
Your battle against the Scoopers is real.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.830
So it's been imaginary 
since the bubble appeared?

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:59.000
We've been living in a 
fantasy world for that long?

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.380
Did I do something bad?

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:05.760
I wouldn't say bad.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.420
This is as shocking... no, even more 
shocking than getting a fever on Halloween

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.350
and being stuck in bed all day.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:13.710
Yeah.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.340
Why are you shocked?

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.150
Because nothing that's 
happened has been real.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.820
Not the customers who came to Park,

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:28.570
or the people who called us 
wonderful, and even Sayumin...

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.120
I don't want to believe this.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.840
But it was all your fantasy.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.810
Then why were we fighting?

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.540
I even thought we killed Sayumin...

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.130
But it was all a lie?

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.510
I don't get what's going on anymore!

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.440
We've been defending a deserted Harajuku.

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:57.760
I can't believe we thought we were 
making the people we imagined happy.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:02.480
I was delighted to hear the 
cheers of my imaginary fans.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.430
Everyone...

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:07.040
What are you so sad about?

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.430
What's wrong with using your imagination?

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:14.110
You can create endless amounts 
of anything with that power.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.000
That's a wonderful thing.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.930
It's not wonderful!

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.480
It's meaningless!

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.840
Yeah. If it's not real, it's meaningless.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.200
I don't understand.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.600
What's wrong with living in a fantasy world?

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.890
What's wrong with that?

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.840
Everything's wrong with it!

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.180
Because it's not real!

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:39.620
I agree, but...

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:45.190
I don't believe everything we've 
done until now wasn't real.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:49.960
Our hearts have been in 
everything we've done.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.080
I don't believe that was fake.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.780
I don't believe the ring 
you're wearing isn't real.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:13.520
Yes, indeed.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.140
You're exactly right, indeed.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.320
What?

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:22.860
This ring is full of the joy I 
experienced while creating it.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:26.460
It's my greatest treasure, indeed.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:28.570
So I know it's not fake.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:35.670
But I didn't feel that way until now.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:40.720
I had no idea that this being a fantasy...

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:44.000
no, a lie would hurt you so much, indeed!

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:50.520
I'm sorry for upsetting you, indeed.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.720
Misa-chan...

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.980
Why are you apologizing, Misa-sama?

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.980
What need is there for us to apologize?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:02.480
Because we made them sad.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:03.890
I don't understand!

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:06.930
I don't understand why they're sad!

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:10.480
They should have fun in their fantasy world!

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:14.280
They don't want that, indeed.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:17.280
It has to be reality. The real world.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:21.150
Yeah. It's meaningless if it's not real.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.660
I'm very sorry, indeed.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:29.090
We'll return to our planet now, indeed.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.600
Wait, Misa-chan.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:39.280
Misa-chan, you just didn't 
understand our feelings

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.800
because of the environment 
you were born into.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.260
I don't think you could help it.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:50.610
So it's okay.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.320
Wait... Rito?

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:58.700
After all, you understand the difference 
between reality and fantasy now.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.470
The importance of things being real.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.330
You understand why we're shocked.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.750
Yes, indeed.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.990
I see. You're right.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.070
But...

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:16.130
I was confused, too, until a minute ago.

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:18.720
I didn't know what was most important.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.630
But now I know.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:25.690
I know what's most important to us.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.650
Finding out this was all 
imaginary was a shock,

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:35.840
but the things we've felt 
until now were real.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:39.620
That's what's most important.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:43.080
Rito-chan...

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:49.550
You don't think the joy and happiness 
you felt was fake, do you?

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.290
I guess not.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.510
That wasn't fake.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:59.640
Then who cares if it's fake or 
fantasy as long as you had fun?

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:03.600
But we fought needlessly 
because of that fantasy.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.350
And we said terrible things to Rito-chan.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:09.960
You don't understand how we feel.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.780
No, I don't.

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:19.100
Misa-chan, when you said you wanted to 
be wonderful, you meant that, didn't you?

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.700
Yes, indeed.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.880
Those feelings weren't fake, were they?

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:25.210
I don't think so.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.290
Misa-chan, you don't have to go.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:30.750
Everyone...

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:35.220
My chest feels tight.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:38.740
What a strange feeling, indeed.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:42.060
Misa-sama? Why are you crying?

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.060
You can just shut up.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:48.420
I didn't have creativity.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:51.560
Even if your fantasy wasn't real,

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:55.610
I still think you're wonderful, indeed.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:57.380
Misa-chan...

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:02.290
Misa-chan, I'm sure you have the 
power to be creative now, too.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.620
So let's make stuff together here.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:06.520
Yeah.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:07.590
You're right.

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:12.570
Harajuku accepts all people 
who want to be wonderful.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:16.510
Even if you're a Scooper, 
you shouldn't have a problem.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:19.150
So don't go, Misa-chan.

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.800
Let's make cute accessories together again.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:26.890
I don't want to leave, either, indeed.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.520
But I'm a Scooper.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:35.800
We've already stolen so many 
things from this planet, indeed.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:42.820
I don't want to cause you 
any more trouble, indeed.

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:46.620
You can just return the things you've stolen.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:47.800
Yeah.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:48.710
I agree.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:51.540
Everyone...

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:57.710
I love you and Harajuku, indeed.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:02.260
What in the world are you talking about?

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.980
What are you talking about?

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:05.860
I'm so furious, I said it twice!

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:07.740
And Misa-sama, I can't believe you, either!

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:12.190
Scoopers are meant to steal. How could 
you allow your heart to be stolen?

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:14.460
You're not worthy of the name Scooper.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.820
You're a contaminant that 
will destroy our kind!

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:23.160
Misa-sama... no, Princess, 
I have lost hope in you.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:27.790
You're no longer the princess of the Scoopers!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:32.780
What's happening?

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.740
Is that supposed to be a shachihoko?

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:43.610
I'm not sure.

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:46.060
His anger probably raised 
his body temperature,

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:50.020
activating his red hot cells 
and causing them to expand...

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.590
Don't bother with the analysis, Kotoko.

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:56.940
The fried shrimp got mad, and for some reason, 
that made it a fried shachihoko, right?

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.380
What are you going to do to us?

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:05.950
Now that you have discovered our 
identity and refuse to join us...

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.250
Stop, Ebifurya!

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:14.830
After spending time with them, 
I've learned something, indeed.

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:19.380
It's not that we couldn't create, 
we just never tried to, indeed!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:24.260
If we try, I'm sure that we can, indeed.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:28.140
And that's even more fun 
than stealing, indeed!

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:32.980
I see there's no point in 
discussing things any further!

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:35.750
Misa-sama, I won't listen to you anymore!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.850
You are not a Scooper!

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.830
You've been poisoned by this planet!

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:44.540
I created this bubble so we could 
focus on this neighborhood,

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.780
but my plan seems to have backfired.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:51.370
Come to think of it, if Harajuku's been 
destroyed and there's nobody here,

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.780
what's going on outside the bubble?

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:57.540
Tokyo Tower was attacked 
by the Scoopers too, right?

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.510
I wonder what happened to those people.

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:02.780
Misa-chan, what's going on outside the bubble?

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:05.260
Um... I don't know, either, indeed.

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:11.030
My fellow Scoopers have no 
doubt stolen what they wanted.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:12.580
No way...

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.350
Don't brag about that!

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:19.560
Now that you know our secrets, 
I can't leave you here.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:23.740
I'll pack you up while you're still 
fresh and quickly take you back!

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:25.420
Know your secrets?

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:27.320
You told us everything yourself.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:28.960
Don't waste your breath!

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.300
Run, indeed!

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:34.790
Stop!

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:37.180
Where can we run to, though?

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:40.710
There's no one in this city who can help us.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.300
There might still be people outside.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:47.220
I'm sure the odds of that aren't zero.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:51.000
Then we can't allow ourselves 
to be captured here.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.740
In that case...

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:54.160
Let's head this way!

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:56.180
You cannot escape!

00:13:56.450 --> 00:14:00.020
There's nowhere to run inside this bubble!

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.260
Ugh, he won't give up!

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:04.260
Kotoko, which way?

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:05.650
This way!

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:11.120
If we go straight, we'll run 
into the bubble, indeed!

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:13.810
We'll head into an alley before we get there!

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:16.040
Stop!

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:26.050
At this rate, the shrimp's 
bound to head this way, so...

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:28.550
This way!

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.430
Where did you go?!

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:08.020
This path ends at the bubble wall, too.

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.980
Yeah, I know.

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:15.920
If we keep heading this 
way to avoid the wall,

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:17.890
won't we run into the shrimp again?

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:21.000
Don't worry. We'll turn before then.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.820
Everyone, I'm sorry, indeed.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:29.930
It's okay.

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:32.430
We won't let that shachihoko catch us.

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:33.800
Let's do our best to escape.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.080
Indeed.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:37.850
This alley leads to a major street.

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:38.790
Keep it up!

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.220
Kotoko, which way now?

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:56.890
Give me a second...

00:15:57.900 --> 00:15:59.770
If you don't hurry, he'll catch up.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:05.610
If we keep running, there's a 100% chance 
he'll catch up to us in ten minutes.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:08.660
We need to come up with another plan.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:11.860
Where are you?!

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:16.240
I'll stop him, indeed.

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:18.420
No, Misa-chan.

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:20.310
He's too dangerous right now.

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:24.670
But you can't fight without 
the Amatsumara, indeed.

00:16:25.220 --> 00:16:27.180
Yeah, but...

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:29.430
Is there any other way?

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:33.920
Jeez... If only the roads would move!

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:35.140
That's it!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:35.720
Huh?

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:41.350
This Harajuku is a product 
of our imaginations, right?

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:45.000
So we might be able to change it.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.100
You're right.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.300
You think we can do that?

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:52.190
Yeah. I have a feeling you can do it, indeed.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:54.530
Let's try praying to that.

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:55.800
You're right.

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:59.890
As long as we're making it, 
let's create our ideal city.

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:01.860
Rito, you're in charge of the design.

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:02.620
Got it.

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:06.210
Who decided the main street 
should be straight?

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:09.030
When the stores you want to 
go to are on opposite ends,

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:11.190
it's a pain to have to walk back and forth.

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:15.700
Then maybe we should 
create a circular street.

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:19.680
Okay. Rito, make the main street circular.

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:24.520
Maybe it should be a little 
bumpy instead of simply round.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.140
Circular and bumpy...

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:28.970
Why don't we flesh out the back alleys, too?

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:30.830
I think it'd be wonderful to find

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:33.840
a great new store down a street 
you accidentally wander down.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.240
Let's do it!

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:42.160
You really are wonderful, indeed!

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.120
It's done.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.520
This is...

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.940
It's great!

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:49.130
There's no time. Let's go.

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:57.290
That's odd.

00:17:57.290 --> 00:18:00.120
I should have caught up to them by now.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:02.550
Where did they go?

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:17.840
That shrimp is just wandering in circles.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.700
Why hasn't he noticed yet?

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:23.610
Ebifurya was only interested in stealing,

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:26.790
so he never took a proper 
look at the city, indeed.

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:28.380
What an idiot.

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:32.700
He can just keep going in circles forever.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:36.050
The map of the new city 
is wonderful, indeed!

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:36.960
Isn't it?

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:40.000
This city is ours.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.850
What a great idea this was.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.490
It's our turn to strike back.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.360
That's odd.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:19:00.340
I don't remember this street...

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:01.180
Hey!

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:06.120
What? You're up there?

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:09.330
You won't escape this time!

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:19.640
What's this?

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.800
Now's our chance!

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:36.240
<b>Great Luck</b>

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:37.950
We did it!

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.600
A great success!

00:19:41.230 --> 00:19:43.700
Wait. Look at that.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:55.630
Everyone... Now you've made me mad.

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:58.590
He turned into a boiled shrimp!

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:06.880
You'll pay for this!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:13.810
Scary shrimp, scary shrimp...

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:19.730
This is...

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.700
Now you've done it!

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:24.520
He figured it out!

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.580
It didn't work, indeed.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:28.990
Unfortunately, no.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.120
Stop!

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:33.610
What should we do?

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:36.670
We have a 0% chance of escaping!

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:38.340
We have to run, though.

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:40.090
If we give up, it's all over.

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:41.450
Okay.

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:42.190
Yeah.

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:43.300
Indeed.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:50.480
This way!

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:58.200
We're trapped.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:00.170
Should we change the streets again?

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:02.190
We don't have time for that.

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:04.070
Then what should we do?

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:06.820
I've got you cornered!

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:09.650
You caused me quite a bit of trouble!

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:11.380
Isn't there anywhere to run?

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:12.780
I'm thinking.

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:13.500
What do we do?

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:17.040
Now, hold still while I capture you!

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:19.870
I won't let you, indeed!

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:20.300
Misa-chan!

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:22.560
Very well.

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:26.990
I'll defeat you and become 
the leader of the Scoopers!

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:32.120
I'll protect the three of them, indeed!

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:37.300
Is that...

00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:38.460
The Amatsumara?

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:41.580
Maybe Misa-chan's Amatsumara 
is responding to her.

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:46.450
How could an Amatsumara 
respond to a Scooper?

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:54.500
You won't beat me, indeed!

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:26.070
Ugh...

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:28.170
Were you that shocked to 
learn you're a tempura shrimp?

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:31.140
I don't know who I am anymore.

00:23:31.140 --> 00:23:34.390
Why did I start calling myself Ebifurya?

00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:36.930
Probably because you thought it sounded cute!

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Illustrated by NC Teikoku</b>
